implement fallbacks for both Quaternions and Planes. However, for Planes, if we fall back to Plane(0, 0, 0, 0) when it is infinite, the test fails. And 3D view port grid is broken and spamming error `ERROR: Condition \"!res\" is true. Returning: false at: create_frustum_points (servers\\rendering\\rendering_light_culler.cpp:648)`\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nSUBCASE(\"is_position_in_frustum\") {\r\n\t// If the point is behind the near plane, it is outside the camera frustum.\r\n\t// So offset1 is not in frustum.\r\n\tCHECK_FALSE(test_camera->is_position_in_frustum(test_camera->get_global_position() + offset1));\r\n\t// If |right| > 5 / 2 or |up| > 2.5 / 2, the point is outside the camera frustum.\r\n\t// So offset2 is in frustum and offset3 and offset4 are not.\r\n\tCHECK(test_camera->is_position_in_frustum(test_camera->get_global_position() + offset2));\r\n\tCHECK_FALSE(test_camera->is_position_in_frustum(test_camera->get_global_position() + offset3));\r\n\tCHECK_FALSE(test_camera->is_position_in_frustum(test_camera->get_global_position() + offset4));\r\n\t// offset5 is beyond the far plane, so it is not in frustum.\r\n\tCHECK_FALSE(test_camera->is_position_in_frustum(test_camera->get_global_position() + offset5)); // <- Failed. offset5 = 10000.0f.\r\n}\r\n```\r\n```\r\nTEST CASE:  [SceneTree][Camera3D] Position queries\r\n  Orthogonal projection\r\n  is_position_in_frustum\r\n\r\n./tests/scene/test_camera_3d.h:180: ERROR: CHECK_FALSE( test_camera->is_position_in_frustum(test_camera->get_global_position() + offset5) ) is NOT correct!\r\n  values: CHECK_FALSE( true )\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think this relates to testing the camera's far plane, but I'm not familiar with the details in camera's view space. @lyuma @clayjohn Do you have any ideas?","created_at":"2026-02-18T13:59:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T04:22:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116427#discussion_r2822504086","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116427","_links